title Season G sixteenth rung — the sealed session, second composition (Comlink confidentiality)
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first past BUHR — Rye prioritized, Glow on green-witnessed Rye; read REMEMBER, the 1024-round itinerary, the six-season double-seat, and the rye-first crypto parity wave; send each finished increment to origin and xykj61; stop at custody gates.
think Second lap of this loop. The signed carry (fifteenth rung) answered "who made this record" — integrity and provenance, in the clear. Its own recommend line named the twin crux: a keyed AEAD-sealed carry over X25519-agreed session keys for Comlink. The decision wave doc frames X25519 as "lets two keepers agree a shared secret before they trust each other — Comlink session keys, Vault sealed storage"; the 1024-round itinerary's Comlink session surface and Season 3 Journey 9 both stand on exactly this shape.
think Lindy-first crux-first: confidentiality between keepers is the other half of the identity story (provenance + confidentiality), foundational to Comlink, Vault, and any two Ponds. Non-gated (TEST keypairs; the frame is held in memory, sent nowhere). De-risked because it authors NO new cryptography — pure composition over THREE already-parity-GREEN primitives: X25519, BLAKE2b-512, ChaCha20-Poly1305.
think Design (self-approved): the standard NaCl-style seal-to-a-public-key box, our own Rye over our own primitives. The one rule ChaCha20-Poly1305 must keep is nonce-uniqueness under a key. A fixed session key across messages would demand a nonce counter and shared state; instead the box takes a FRESH ephemeral keypair per message (the caller supplies the randomness — the library invents no entropy), so shared = X25519(esk, recipient_pub) is one-message, and one BLAKE2b-512 over (shared | epk | recipient_pub) yields BOTH the 32-byte key AND the 12-byte nonce — fresh key and fresh nonce every message, no reuse possible. The recipient's public key is fed as AEAD authenticated data so a frame sealed to one keeper cannot be replayed to another; the sender's long-term identity never appears (a sealed box is anonymous by construction).
think Frame: magic GSS1 | epk(32) | cipher-len(u64 BE) | ciphertext | Poly1305 tag(16). seal builds it in place in the caller's out buffer (allocation-free, bounded by the AEAD's own 64 KiB message bound). open rederives shared = X25519(recipient_priv, epk), rederives key+nonce, and returns a zero-copy plaintext slice ONLY when the AEAD tag verifies.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal pass — no correction needed, the second first-pass GREEN this loop. Ten selftest blocks: round-trip across seven plaintext lengths (empty through 64 KiB max), the ciphertext proven NOT equal to the plaintext (the message is truly enciphered), the SEALED-BOX FRESHNESS property (two different ephemerals sealing the same plaintext to the same recipient yield different frames that both still open to the same message — what makes reuse-free sealing safe), determinism given a fixed ephemeral, and six refusals: a wrong recipient (keeper C cannot open a frame sealed to keeper B), a tampered ciphertext, a tampered tag, and a tampered ephemeral key all fail OpenFailed revealing no plaintext, plus bad magic and two truncations and an undersized buffer.
obs tame_style_check bans clean; crypto/sealed_session.rye lands in none of the ratchet lists. Honest scope held: purely local over TEST keypairs — no real identity key, no network, no funds, no real device. Named the caller's randomness duty plainly (the ephemeral private must be fresh in real use; the selftest uses deterministic TEST ephemerals to prove the mathematics). Constant-time timing-safety stays the Season's named horizon (unchanged in the composed primitives), and agreeing a session with the maintainer's own identity key stays the custody gate. No gate crossed.
loom witness=crypto_sealed_session_selftest primitives_composed=3 plaintext_lengths=7 refusal_paths=6 result=GREEN
file crypto/sealed_session.rye the sealed session carry authored in pure Rye — pure composition over GREEN X25519 + BLAKE2b-512 + ChaCha20-Poly1305, sealed-box shape, GREEN on first metal pass
file work-in-progress/REMEMBER.md living edge advanced to SIXTEEN rungs (fourteen primitives + two compositions); sealed_session rung prepended, signed_carry relabeled prior
file session-logs/README.md newest-first row for this rung
recommend check-in (Claude) — two non-gated crypto compositions landed and sent this loop (provenance + confidentiality); the crypto library now spans fourteen parity-GREEN primitives and two composed carries. The next natural crux is a Kumara identity descriptor (binding a signer key to a name) or a Vault sealed-at-rest store, both of which begin to touch the identity/custody seam — a good checkpoint for a design ruling before opening that surface, since signing/sealing with the maintainer's own key is the gate.
